CODEGEN.md §2.9, DECISIONS 336: an export fn returning String? is a well-placed @text (it reports nothing); only the @text on a let beside it is E8021 position.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Doc.
@text("v.sql")
export fn v() -> String? { return "x" }

/// Doc.
@text("w.sql")
let w: String = "SELECT 1;"

emit text { out: "@generated/sql" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8021]  a/a.canon:8:1
  @text belongs on a public package-level export fn with no parameter, returning String or a value with a wire form

